        <p>Date Passed: Monday, May 23, 2016</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, June 30, 2016</p><p>ORD C35389 Section 7</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.040.110">Section 17F.040.110</a> Unsafe Buildings<br />
        <p>Substandard and unsafe buildings are subject to the regulations provided in <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Chapter=17F.070">chapter 17F.070 SMC</a>.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 28, 2005</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, April 2, 2005</p><p>ORD C33594 Section 3</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.040.120">Section 17F.040.120</a> REPEALED (Roof Design)<br />
        <p>Repealed by Ordinance C34600</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 7, 2010</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, July 1, 2010</p><p>ORD C34600 Section 5</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.040.125">Section 17F.040.125</a> REPEALED (Alternating Tread Devices)<br />
        <p>
        	Repealed by ORD C35389<o:p></o:p></p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, May 23, 2016</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, June 30, 2016</p><p>ORD C35389 Section 8</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.040.130">Section 17F.040.130</a> Special Skywalk Provisions<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Definitions.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&ldquo;Skywalk area&rdquo; is those areas within a building through which pedestrians may pass when en route from any skywalk bridge or vertical circulation point to another skywalk bridge or vertical circulation point.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">On single-tenant floors this includes the entire floor.</span></span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="2" style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">On multi-tenant floors this includes all areas which are not separated from the pedestrian routes by walls, doors, windows, chain gates, rolling grilles or other devices.</span></span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&ldquo;Skywalk bridge&rdquo; is any elevated bridge-like structure connecting two buildings and primarily designed for pedestrian use.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&ldquo;Skywalk system&rdquo; is the entirety of the central business district interconnecting above the street-level pedestrian circulation system.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Required Separations.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Required building separations must be in accordance with IBC Section 707. Openings for the purpose of interconnecting the skywalk areas of buildings may occur so long as they be protected as required by IBC Section 707 for area separation walls. The protection may be provided by any labeled fire door assembly of the proper rating.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Exceptions:</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Protection of openings in walls between buildings of like construction types need not be provided if the buildings are sprinklered on the floors upon which the openings occur.</span></span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="2" style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Protection of openings in walls between buildings of unlike construction types may be reduced from the required three-hour rating to a two-hour rating and from a one-and-one-half-hour rating to a one-hour rating if the buildings are sprinklered on the floors upon which the openings occur.</span></span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Exits.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Each building connected to the skywalk system by opening(s) or skywalk bridge(s) must have exits as required by the IBC.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Exceptions:</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:80px; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">After business hours skywalk areas and tenant areas within a building may be closed off from each other or the rest of the building by security devices, but:</span></span></span></span></p>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Skywalk areas must be served by at least one exit at all times, and</span></span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="2" style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Tenant spaces must be served by at least one exit at all times. This exit may be into the skywalk area, but openings with closures other than leaf-type doors are not considered as exits after business hours. Proper separation of exits must be maintained in cases where two exits are required.</span></span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="4" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Corridors.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Skywalk areas within buildings are treated as corridors subject to the requirements of IBC Section 1020.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Exceptions:</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">When thirty feet or more in width, such areas are not treated as corridors.</span></span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="2" style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">When the skywalk area is fully sprinklered and smoke alarms are installed, the corridor walls may be of noncombustible construction instead of one-hour construction so long as sprinklers are installed on both sides of the corridor wall. Openings in the wall must be equipped with self-closing or automatic-closing (IBC Section 716) doors with gaskets in the frames. Only openings glazed with safety glazing or wire glass are permitted but there is no limit on the amount of glazing.</span></span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="3" style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">When the skywalk areas and the tenant space opening onto it are both fully sprinklered and smoke alarms are installed, no corridor walls or doors are required. If walls are provided, they must be of noncombustible construction.</span></span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">In no case are partitions, rails, counters and similar space dividers construed to form corridor walls.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, May 23, 2016</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, June 30, 2016</p><p>ORD C35389 Section 9</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.040.140">Section 17F.040.140</a> Awnings<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">In addition to the requirements of IBC Section 3105, these provisions apply:</span></span></span></span></p>
        
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">An awning which defines an entrance to a nonresidential use and which provides shelter between a passenger loading point and the entrance may be installed in accordance with the standards of this section so long as any portion of the awning that does not project at least forty-two inches over the pedestrian way is confined along the facade to a width not to exceed the width of the doorway plus six feet on both sides.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Projection.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:40px; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Awnings may extend over public property (whether the building is conforming or nonconforming) but no portion shall extend nearer than two feet to the face of the nearest curb line measured horizontally.</span></span></span></p>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">An awning which projects more than eighteen inches into the public right-of-way must provide a minimum forty-two-inch coverage over any sidewalk adjacent to the property.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="4" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Clearance.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:40px; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">All portions of any awning shall be at least eight but not more than twelve feet above any public walkway.</span></span></span></p>
        
        <p style="margin-left:40px; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">EXCEPTION: Any valance attached to an awning shall not project above the roof of the awning at the point of attachment and shall not extend more than twelve inches below the roof of the awning at the point of attachment, but in no case shall any portion of a valance be less than seven feet in height above a public way.</span></span></span></span></p>
        
        <ol start="5" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Signs.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:40px; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">If an awning also carries advertising copy, the copy is regulated as a sign, but the awning is not thereby exempted from the provisions of this chapter as provided in Section 3107</span></span></span></p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 29, 2021</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, May 6, 2021</p><p>ORD C36026 Section 2</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.040.150">Section 17F.040.150</a> Building Inspector – Building Official<br />
        <p>The building official is the officer charged with the administration and enforcement of the building and other construction codes or his/her duly authorized representative. The building inspector is the building official or a designated employee.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 28, 2005</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, April 2, 2005</p><p>ORD C33594 Section 3</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.040.160">Section 17F.040.160</a> Functions of Building Inspector<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">The building inspector has responsibility to:</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
        
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">process applications for licenses and permits;</span></span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">review and approve plans, specifications, diagrams and drawings;</span></span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">conduct inspections of work sites, work in progress and buildings;</span></span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="4" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">make and promulgate rules, regulations and interpretations of the building code;</span></span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="5" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">initiate proceedings, including prosecutions, to enforce the building code;</span></span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="6" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">maintain records of all permits issued and of all other administrative activities under the building code;</span></span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="7" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">provide clerical and technical assistance to the construction review board, as provided in&nbsp;</span></span></span><span style="color:black"><a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Chapter=04.06"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">chapter 4.06 SMC</span></span></span></a></span><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black"> and</span></span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="8" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Issue civil infractions to enforce any violation of this chapter.</span></span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, July 26, 2021</p><p>Effective Date: Friday, July 2, 2021</p><p>ORD C36091 Section 9</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.040.170">Section 17F.040.170</a> Fire Official<br />
        <ol type="A">
        <li>The fire official, as defined in <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=17F.080.040">SMC 17F.080.040</a>, reviews and approves plans and specifications submitted for a building permit.<br />&nbsp; 
        <li>In addition to any building permit, the fire official reviews plans, issues permits and inspects for the installation of fire protection and fire detection equipment.<br />&nbsp; 
        <li>The fire official has permit and inspection responsibility for a number of uses and occupancies of buildings as provided in IFC Section 105. </li></ol>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 17, 2013</p><p>Effective Date: Monday, July 1, 2013</p><p>ORD C34993 Section 2</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.040.180">Section 17F.040.180</a> Hearing Officer – Construction Review Board<br />
        <p>The hearing officer and construction review board have jurisdiction over the building code as provided in <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Chapter=04.06">chapter 4.06 SMC</a>.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 28, 2005</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, April 2, 2005</p><p>ORD C33594 Section 3</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.040.190">Section 17F.040.190</a> Unapproved Work<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Whenever the inspector finds materials used or work performed which does not conform to this code, the inspector rejects the work and orders the permittee, in person or by phone, and later in writing if requested, to make all corrections in materials and workmanship necessary to satisfy this code within fifteen days, or within such longer time as the inspector may grant for good cause, unless the permittee timely appeals to the hearing officer.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Whenever the inspector finds any building or structure:</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">being used or maintained in a dangerous or unsafe condition; or</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">being constructed, demolished, altered or extended without a proper permit or by an unauthorized person;</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:40px; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">the inspector notifies the building official. The building official gives written notice to the owners of the premises and the contractor to take corrective action in a specified time.</span></span></span></span></p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 28, 2005</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, April 2, 2005</p><p>ORD C33594 Section 3</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.040.200">Section 17F.040.200</a> Emergency Exemptions for Housing for Indigent Persons<br />
        <p>Pursuant to RCW 19.27.042 and WAC 51.16.030, the City exempts from the state building code requirements buildings whose character of use or occupancy has been changed in order to provide housing for indigent persons. The character of use or occupancy of an existing building located within the City may be changed in order to provide housing for indigent persons without conforming to all of the requirements of the State Building Code provided that: </p>
        <ol type="A">
        <li>the city building official has reviewed and approved the proposed exemption; and<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>the proposed housing for indigent persons is less hazardous than the existing use; and<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>any code deficiencies exempted pose no threat to human life, health or safety; and<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>the building or buildings exempted are owned or administered by a public agency or nonprofit corporation; and<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>the exemption is authorized for no more than five years, subject to renewal of the exemption by the building official.</li></ol>
        <p>The adoption of this ordinance for the purpose to provide for occupancy exemptions for indigent housing as outlined in this section shall not be considered a local government residential amendment requiring approval by the State Building Code Council.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, December 5, 2005</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, January 8, 2006</p><p>ORD C33772 Section 1</p>				<p><a href="/smc/?Chapter=17F.050">Chapter 17F.050</a> Electrical Code</p>
        					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.050.010">Section 17F.050.010</a> Adoption of the National Electrical Code<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The National Electrical Code, current adopted<u> </u>Edition, as published by the National Fire Protection Association, is the electrical code for the City.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The rules and regulations of the State department of labor and industries, contained in chapter 296-46B WAC (except WAC 296-46B-906, WAC 296- 46B-907, WAC 296-46B-908, WAC 296-46B-909, and WAC 296-46B- 911) are adopted as amendments and interpretations of the National Electrical Code.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Persons doing electrical work are also required to comply with the state electrical installations laws.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="4" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The National Electrical Code is further modified by the local amendments as provided in this chapter.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, May 11, 2020</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, June 14, 2020</p><p>ORD C35899 Section 7</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.050.020">Section 17F.050.020</a> Permit Required<br />
        <p>
        <ol type="A">
        <li>No person may place, install, alter, change, add to, or cause or allow to be installed, altered, changed or added, any wires, apparatus or fixtures for the use of electricity in any building without first obtaining an electrical permit. A person must obtain a separate permit for each job.<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>When an emergency demands that work be done immediately, the person doing the work is required to notify the electrical inspector as soon as possible in the morning of the first working day following the emergency in order that an inspection be made and a permit be processed. </li></ol>
        <p></p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 28, 2005</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, April 2, 2005</p><p>ORD C33594 Section 4</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.050.030">Section 17F.050.030</a> Plans and Specifications<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li>An applicant for an electrical permit must furnish, subject to modification or waiver by the electrical inspector in appropriate cases, a set of wiring plans and specifications, or a wiring schedule, with respect to wiring in excess of two hundred amperes, single phase, or one hundred fifty amperes, three phase. The building official may require that plans, computations and specifications be prepared by an electrical engineer licensed by Washington state.</li>
        	<li>
        	<p>The applicant must render the plan:</p>
        
        	<ol>
        		<li>
        		<p>to scale;</p>
        		</li>
        		<li>
        		<p>upon substantial paper;</p>
        		</li>
        		<li>
        		<p>with sufficient clarity to indicate the location, nature and extent of the proposed work;</p>
        		</li>
        		<li>so as to show in detail that the work will comply with the code and all other pertinent laws.</li>
        	</ol>
        
        	<p>Specifications may be on the plan or on separate sheets in indelible form.</p>
        	</li>
        	<li>
        	<p>The applicant must indicate:</p>
        
        	<ol>
        		<li>
        		<p>the type, rating and location of any new service equipment;</p>
        		</li>
        		<li>
        		<p>for each feeder, a diagram or schedule showing:</p>
        
        		<ol style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li>
        			<p>size of feeder switch;</p>
        			</li>
        			<li>
        			<p>size of feeder conductors;</p>
        			</li>
        			<li>
        			<p>size of feeder raceway;</p>
        			</li>
        			<li>
        			<p>location of panel boards or load center;</p>
        			</li>
        			<li>
        			<p>type of occupancy;</p>
        			</li>
        			<li>
        			<p>area served;</p>
        			</li>
        			<li>
        			<p>all special loads;</p>
        			</li>
        			<li>
        			<p>total computed load for lighting, appliances and motors determined as specified in the National Electrical Code.</p>
        			</li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        		<li>
        		<p>on the panelboard or load center schedule for each panel:</p>
        
        		<ol style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li>
        			<p>bus-bar capacity,</p>
        			</li>
        			<li>
        			<p>voltage rating and phase,</p>
        			</li>
        			<li>
        			<p>number and type of circuit protective devices,</p>
        			</li>
        			<li>wattage or ampere requirements for each circuit.<br />
        			&nbsp;</li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        	<li>The applicant must show short circuit fault currents on riser diagrams to indicate compliance with Sections 110-9, 110-10 and Article 240 of the National Electrical Code.</li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 28, 2005</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, April 2, 2005</p><p>ORD C33594 Section 4</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.050.040">Section 17F.050.040</a> Materials<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li>No person may use in the installation, alteration or extension of wiring or fixtures in any building material or equipment not of a type conforming with all applicable standards of the United States Department of Commerce, National Bureau of Standards, or of Underwriters&rsquo; Laboratories, or of another nationally recognized testing laboratory.</li>
        	<li>
        	<p>A person may use material or equipment not labeled or listed as complying with the standards of subsection (A) of this section if:</p>
        
        	<ol>
        		<li>
        		<p>consisting of approved components; and</p>
        		</li>
        		<li>
        		<p>the approved components have been inter-connected and enclosed in accordance with the National Electrical Code; or</p>
        		</li>
        		<li>
        		<p>clearly appearing to meet the safety standards established by recognized testing laboratories for similar material or equipment; and</p>
        		</li>
        		<li>installed in a manner and for the purpose prescribed.<br />
        		&nbsp;</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        	<li>Electrical metallic tubing (E.M.T.) shall not be used for grounding when installed in concrete, under concrete in grouted wall cavities, or in the earth, unless covered by an approved and listed corrosion protection covering, including any elbows, couplings and fittings as required by Section 358-1 of the National Electrical Code.<br />
        	&nbsp;</li>
        	<li>Terminals on the load side of a four-hundred-amp meter socket shall utilize only one lug suitable for use with one or more conductors.<br />
        	&nbsp;</li>
        	<li>Where gutters are used at the service location, they shall not be less than six-inch by six-inch size.</li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 28, 2005</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, April 2, 2005</p><p>ORD C33594 Section 4</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.050.050">Section 17F.050.050</a> Alteration and Repair<br />
        <p>
        <ol type="A">
        <li>All work of alteration, addition or repair must comply with the requirements of this code for material, equipment and installation. Alteration, addition or repair does not require upgrading or retrofitting of all existing wiring and fixtures, so long as the existing installation met the code at the time of installation, except as provided in subsections (B) through (D) of this section.<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>The owner of a building containing wiring which either was improperly modified or has deteriorated or been damaged or overloaded so as to be hazardous must replace, repair or otherwise modify the existing wiring to the point of compliance with this code.<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>If the use or occupancy of the building or part of the building is classified as hazardous, the owner must alter or replace all wiring, apparatus and fixtures as necessary to comply with this code.<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>If the work of alteration or addition will overload existing services and feeders, when loads and diversities are calculated in accordance with this code, the services and feeders, including panel boards, must be increased in ampacity to meet the standards of this code. </li></ol>
        <p></p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 28, 2005</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, April 2, 2005</p><p>ORD C33594 Section 4</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.050.060">Section 17F.050.060</a> REPEALED (Repair of Fire Damage)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C34039.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 4, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, July 1, 2007</p><p>ORD C34039 Section 12</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.050.070">Section 17F.050.070</a> Snap-in Breakers<br />
        <p>Snap-in breakers shall not be used to backfeed a panel or switchboard unless bolted in place where service conductors are connected to the breaker.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 28, 2005</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, April 2, 2005</p><p>ORD C33594 Section 4</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.050.080">Section 17F.050.080</a> Shell Buildings<br />
        <p>In new construction, when the total load is not known due to unfinished future tenant spaces, each set of service entrance conductors shall terminate in a single main disconnect with overload protection.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 28, 2005</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, April 2, 2005</p><p>ORD C33594 Section 4</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.050.090">Section 17F.050.090</a> Installation of Residential Service Entrance<br />
        <ol type="A">
        	<li>
        		<p>
        			The service entrance conductors for a new single-family dwelling having five hundred square feet or more of habitable space must be installed in a raceway of not less than two-inch trade size which terminates in a two-hundred amp cabinet or panel containing a two-hundred amp main breaker or set of fuses. The conductors must be approved for carrying two hundred amperes.</p>
        	</li>
        	<li>
        		<p>
        			The service entrance cable for a new dwelling having less than five hundred square feet of habitable space or for rewiring an existing dwelling of any size may be installed either by the method provided in subsection (A) of this section or as exposed wiring on the exterior of the building, in accordance with the National Electrical Code.</p>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, July 17, 2017</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, August 30, 2017</p><p>ORD C35520 Section 2</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.050.100">Section 17F.050.100</a> Wiring for Construction Use<br />
        <p>A permit and inspection are required for the installation of wiring for construction use, such as to supply power during construction. The inspector may limit the time construction wiring may be used. After inspection and upon approval of the wiring, the inspector notifies the serving utility that connection of the wiring to its distribution system is authorized.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 28, 2005</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, April 2, 2005</p><p>ORD C33594 Section 4</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.050.110">Section 17F.050.110</a> Barricade Lighting<br />
        <p>A person installing lighting in a public passageway which is part of a construction barricade must:</p>
        <ol type="A">
        <li>install the wiring in metal raceways but may use flexible connections where sections of the barricade are to be removed;<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>use lamps of at least one hundred watts;<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>space lamps not more than thirty feet apart;<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>install metal or glass guards over lamps;<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>use red lamps at the extremities of the barricade and at sixty-feet intervals along the vehicular traffic side. </li></ol>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 28, 2005</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, April 2, 2005</p><p>ORD C33594 Section 4</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.050.120">Section 17F.050.120</a> Floodlights, Colored Lights<br />
        <p>No person may install or maintain upon any property a floodlight or intermittent or blinking light so situated as to interfere with the safe flow of traffic by creating a blinding effect or causing the false appearance of a warning, directional, or traffic-control signal.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 28, 2005</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, April 2, 2005</p><p>ORD C33594 Section 4</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.050.130">Section 17F.050.130</a> Inspection<br />
        <p>
        <ol type="A">
        <li>When the work under an electrical permit is complete and ready for inspection, the permittee is required to notify the inspector and to keep the work open for inspection for twenty-four hours, excluding weekends and holidays.<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>The permittee must, upon the direction of the inspector, expose any work which has been prematurely covered or concealed prior to inspection and approval.<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>The inspector causes work to be inspected as soon as reasonably possible after the call for inspection is made. </li></ol>
        <p></p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 28, 2005</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, April 2, 2005</p><p>ORD C33594 Section 4</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.050.140">Section 17F.050.140</a> Unapproved Work<br />
        <ol type="A">
        	<li>
        		<p>
        			Whenever the inspector finds materials used or work performed which does not conform to this code, the inspector rejects the work and orders the permittee, in person or by phone, and later in writing if requested, to make all corrections in materials and workmanship necessary to satisfy this code within fifteen days, or within such longer time as the inspector may grant for good cause, unless the permittee timely appeals to the hearing officer.</p>
        	</li>
        	<li>
        		<p>
        			Whenever the inspector finds any electric wiring, apparatus or fixture:</p>
        		<ol>
        			<li>
        				<p>
        					being used or maintained in a dangerous or unsafe condition; or</p>
        			</li>
        			<li>
        				<p>
        					being installed, altered, or extended without a proper permit or by an unauthorized person;</p>
        			</li>
        		</ol>
        		<p>
        			the inspector gives written notice to the owners of the premises to take corrective action in a specified time.</p>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, July 17, 2017</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, August 30, 2017</p><p>ORD C35520 Section 3</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.050.150">Section 17F.050.150</a> Disconnection of Service<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The electrical inspector disconnects or causes the disconnection of electric service to any installation, conductors, apparatus, or fixtures which remain in an unsafe or dangerous condition following a notice or which have been connected without approval for service.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The fire department may disconnect any electric service when required for fire safety.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Upon disconnection of service the inspector seals the unlawful conductor, apparatus or fixture and/or attaches a notice that service has been disconnected for violation of this code.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="4" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">No person, except the electrical inspector, may remove a seal or notice of disconnection or reconnect any installation which has been disconnected by the electrical inspector or fire department until connection has been approved by the inspector.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="5" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">A Safety inspection by a city electrical inspector will be required to approve a service for reconnection of power by the serving utility company under the following circumstances:</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Power has been off for one year or more</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">When requested by the serving utility company</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Mixed wiring between units</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="4" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Extension cords discovered running between different houses or buildings</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="5" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Vandalized wiring discovered or other noted electrical issues</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="6" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">A safety inspection permit for the purpose of service reconnection may be issued to home owners, realtors, renters, and other persons responsible for a structure for the purpose of a safety inspection only but not for the purpose of inspecting electrical work that has occurred that requires an electrical permit according the requirements of WAC 296-46B.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="7" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The fees for electrical safety permits are found in <a href="/smc/?Section=08.02.031"><span style="color:blue">SMC 08.02.031.(S)</span></a></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="8" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">If the inspector discovers corrections are required before the service can be re-energized, a separate &ldquo;electrical permit&rdquo; will be required by an authorized person. The inspector will inspect the repairs when notified.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, July 14, 2014</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, August 28, 2014</p><p>ORD C35117 Section 3</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.050.160">Section 17F.050.160</a> Underground Loop<br />
        <p>A customer service from the central business district underground loop, when found hazardous due to deterioration or other reasons, must be moved from under the sidewalk area and reinstalled inside the property line, subject to the permit and inspection requirements of this code.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 28, 2005</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, April 2, 2005</p><p>ORD C33594 Section 4</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.050.165">Section 17F.050.165</a> Fixed Outdoor Electric Deicing and Snow-Melting Equipment<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Ground-fault protection of equipment shall be provided in compliance with the National Electric Code for all fixed outdoor electric deicing and snow melting equipment that is embedded in driveways, sidewalks, steps, or other areas that are publically traversable. This requirement shall apply to all embedded systems and shall apply retroactively to systems that were installed under older versions of the National Electrical Code.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">All fixed outdoor electric deicing and snow melting systems shall be maintained by the property owner according to ANSI/IEEE 515.1-2012. Systems located within the public right of way shall be maintained by the adjacent property owner. Testing of the systems shall be conducted by the property owner and shall occur annually.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Property owners with a fixed outdoor electric deicing and snow melting systems located within the adjacent public right of way or on public property shall register the system with the City Engineer on a form approved by the city engineer. The registration shall include a site plan showing the location of the system. In addition to any required permits, registration submittals for new installations shall include manufacturers cut sheets.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, July 1, 2019</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, August 14, 2019</p><p>ORD C35788 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.050.170">Section 17F.050.170</a> Connection of Service<br />
        <p>
        <ol type="A">
        <li>No person may connect or allow to be connected any installation of wiring, apparatus, or fixtures in any building or for construction use until the inspector has approved the connection.<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>A permittee must apply to the inspector for an inspection to be made at the time a cut-over to new service is to be done.<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>Following emergency repairs service may be restored on condition that the electrical inspector be notified in the morning of the next working day. </li></ol>
        <p></p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 28, 2005</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, April 2, 2005</p><p>ORD C33594 Section 4</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.050.180">Section 17F.050.180</a> Electrical Inspector<br />
        <p>The electrical inspector is the building official or a state-qualified employee designated by the building official.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 28, 2005</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, April 2, 2005</p><p>ORD C33594 Section 4</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.050.190">Section 17F.050.190</a> Functions of Electrical Inspector<br />
        <p>
        	The electrical inspector has responsibility to:</p>
        <ol type="A">
        	<li>
        		<p>
        			conduct inspections of installation and equipment;</p>
        	</li>
        	<li>
        		<p>
        			initiate proceedings, including prosecutions, to enforce the electrical code;</p>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, July 17, 2017</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, August 30, 2017</p><p>ORD C35520 Section 4</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.050.200">Section 17F.050.200</a> Hearing Officer<br />
        <p>
        	The hearing officer has jurisdiction over appeals pertaining to the electrical code as provided in <a href="https://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Chapter=17G.070" target="_blank">SMC 17G.050.070</a>.</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, July 17, 2017</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, August 30, 2017</p><p>ORD C35520 Section 5</p>				<p><a href="/smc/?Chapter=17F.060">Chapter 17F.060</a> Elevator Code</p>
        					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.060.010">Section 17F.060.010</a> Adoption of Standard Code<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Chapter 70.87 RCW, Chapter 30 of the International Building Code, and the most current Washington State adopted version of chapter 296-96 WAC and their amendments, as applicable, are the elevator code of the City.</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Exceptions:</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">All fees shall be determined by the City of Spokane and referenced in&nbsp;<a href="https://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=08.02.033">SMC 8.02.033</a>.</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">296-96-01000 WAC &ndash; Permit Process.</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">296-96-01070 WAC &ndash; Violation Penalty Fees.</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, November 26, 2018</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, January 3, 2019</p><p>ORD C35699 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.060.020">Section 17F.060.020</a> Installation Permit<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">No person may construct, erect, place, install, or alter any elevator, dumb waiter, escalator, temporary personnel hoist, platform lift, stair climber, material lift or moving walk or related equipment without first securing a permit from the Development Services Department.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">The applicant for a permit must file with the inspector a copy of the plans and specifications showing details of the new installation or addition to an existing installation. Submitted plans are also reviewed by the Development Services Department for compliance with other adopted codes.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 20, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Friday, November 28, 2025</p><p>ORD C36753 Section 35</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.060.030">Section 17F.060.030</a> Inspection<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The elevator inspector inspects and, as necessary, tests:</span></span></span></span></span></p>
        
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">each installation before the operating permit is issued for initial use; and</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">each temporary personnel hoist semiannually. All other conveyance<u>s</u> annually, except those in private residences.</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">On a random basis, witness testing of conveyances to ensure that testing is being completed according to current codes adopted.</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="4" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Witness all Category 5 hydraulic elevator testing and apply a City of Spokane Seal to all overspeed valves and pressure relief valves.</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="5" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Witness all Category 1 testing and cleaning of all escalators.</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="6" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Failure to arrange to have City Inspector witness the tests shall result in a Class I Civil Infraction.</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, November 26, 2018</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, January 3, 2019</p><p>ORD C35699 Section 3</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.060.040">Section 17F.060.040</a> Requirements<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">All new and existing elevators, dumb waiters, escalators, stair climbers, platform lifts, temporary personnel hoists, material lifts and moving walks and alterations must conform to this code.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">A sidewalk elevator, or hoist, or a freight elevator, which does not rise above the ground floor must have doors and gates so constructed that the car cannot move until they are closed. A sidewalk hoist must be equipped with safety rods so that it cannot be started until the sidewalk doors are open.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Lock boxes for machine room access may be required by conditions.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="4" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Conveyances with uncorrected deficiencies are subject to additional inspections and fees. An elevator inspector may revoke an operating permit and red-tag the conveyance if deficiencies remain uncorrected for one hundred fifty days.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="5" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Elevators no longer used or deemed to be unsafe may be ordered to be decommissioned by the City Inspector.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="6" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Conveyances to be decommissioned must occur by permit and inspections according to the requirements of ASME 17.1. Failure to decommission a conveyance as directed by the elevator inspector shall result in a class I civil infraction.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="7" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Elevators incorporating noncircular elastomeric coated steel suspension members (belt suspension) shall use only fire rated belts tested to UL 62, UL 1581 FT-1 fire rating or equivalent.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, May 11, 2020</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, June 14, 2020</p><p>ORD C35899 Section 8</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.060.050">Section 17F.060.050</a> Operating Permit<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">No person may maintain or operate any elevator, dumb waiter, escalator, temporary personnel hoist, stair climber, platform lift,<u> </u>material lift, or moving walk in the City unless there be in effect an operating permit.</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The owner of the conveyance shall display the current operating permit in the cab of the elevator or the elevator machine room. Operating permits for material and stair lifts shall be posted in-sight and near the conveyance.</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Fees for conveyance operating permits are to be paid annually except for temporary personnel hoists. Temporary personnel hoists are addressed in 17F.060.050(D). The annual inspection may or may not occur at the time of billing for the operating permit.</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="4" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Operating permit fees for temporary personnel hoist are paid semiannually. Semiannual operating permits will be issued if six-month inspections are current. </span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, November 26, 2018</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, January 3, 2019</p><p>ORD C35699 Section 5</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.060.060">Section 17F.060.060</a> Dangerous Conveyances<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Whenever the elevator inspector finds a conveyance or part dangerous or unsafe, the owner must immediately repair, replace or otherwise correct the danger.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">No person may: </span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">remove, conceal or deface any notice of condemnation posted on a conveyance by the inspector; or </span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">operate a conveyance until it has been inspected and approved for operation by the inspector. </span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">remove any lock or lock out device that has been placed on a conveyance by an authorized person that is intended to prevent the operation of the conveyance that has been deemed unsafe to operate by that person.</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Violation of this section will result in a Class I civil infraction assessed daily until corrected.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, May 11, 2020</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, June 14, 2020</p><p>ORD C35899 Section 9</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.060.070">Section 17F.060.070</a> REPEALED (Modernization)<br />
        <p>Repealed</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, August 14, 2006</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, September 27, 2006</p><p>ORD C33901 Section 25</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.060.080">Section 17F.060.080</a> Elevator Inspector<br />
        <p>The elevator inspector is the building official or a state-qualified employee designated by the building official.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 28, 2005</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, April 2, 2005</p><p>ORD C33594 Section 5</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.060.090">Section 17F.060.090</a> Functions of Elevator Inspector<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The elevator inspector is responsible to:</span></span></span></span></span></p>
        
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">ensure all conveyances are maintained, inspected, and safety tested at least once a year (except temporary personnel hoists which are safety inspected semiannually), according to the guidelines of this chapter and the standards adopted by the state per chapter 70.87 RCW and WAC 296-96; </span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">review and approve plans for construction, installation, and alteration of conveyances except stair climbers;</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">conduct inspections and tests of conveyances;</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="4" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">issue, suspend, and revoke operating permits;</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="5" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">make and promulgate rules, regulations, and interpretations of the elevator code;</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="6" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">initiate proceedings, including prosecutions, to enforce the elevator code;&nbsp;</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="7" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">maintain records of all permits issued and of all inspections made.</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, November 26, 2018</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, January 3, 2019</p><p>ORD C35699 Section 6</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.060.100">Section 17F.060.100</a> Appeals<br />
        <p>Resolutions of disputes will be settled through the procedures set forth in RCW 70.87.205 as prescribed for municipalities having their own elevator code.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 7, 2010</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, July 1, 2010</p><p>ORD C34600 Section 24</p>				<p><a href="/smc/?Chapter=17F.070">Chapter 17F.070</a> Existing Building and Conservation Code</p>
        					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.070.010">Section 17F.070.010</a> In General<br />
        <ol type="A">
        	<li>
        		<p>
        			Generally, this title does not apply retroactively so as to require owners of buildings to replace, alter, or retrofit portions of buildings or systems within buildings to comply fully with the current code standards. As stated in the International Building Code, the Washington State Amendments, and the International Existing Building Code, only new work of addition, alteration, repair, and new installations need comply with the current codes so long as:</p>
        		<ol>
        			<li>
        				<p>
        					the work complied with the codes in effect at the time;</p>
        			</li>
        			<li>
        				<p>
        					the building, equipment, and devices have been maintained in a safe and sanitary condition;</p>
        			</li>
        			<li>
        				<p>
        					there is no change in use, occupancy, or load as would violate the current codes; and</p>
        			</li>
        			<li>
        				<p>
        					the building or premises or part thereof has not become dangerous.</p>
        			</li>
        		</ol>
        	</li>
        	<li>
        		<p>
        			Conversely, every owner and occupant of premises is under a continuous obligation to prevent the property from becoming a nuisance and to maintain property in a reasonably safe condition.</p>
        	</li>
        	<li>
        		<p>
        			It is the purpose of this chapter, therefore, to:</p>
        		<ol>
        			<li>
        				<p>
        					specify the minimum maintenance and rehabilitation standards for all buildings and properties necessary to prevent blight and such environmental degradation as would jeopardize the health and safety of occupants and the community, as authorized by chapter 35.80 RCW and the general police power of the City; and</p>
        			</li>
        			<li>
        				<p>
        					adopt specific retroactive requirements necessary to provide reasonable safety to the occupants of buildings, which present special hazards; namely, apartment and hotel buildings over two stories in height.</p>
        			</li>
        		</ol>
        	</li>
        	<li>
        		<p>
        			It is further the policy of the City to put vacant buildings to use, especially residences, by encouraging the rehabilitation of usable structures and to demolish those that are beyond repair so that new development can occur.</p>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, May 23, 2016</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, June 30, 2016</p><p>ORD C35389 Section 10</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.070.020">Section 17F.070.020</a> Terminology<br />
        <p>Words and phrases in this chapter are defined in reference to the building code and the fire code.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 28, 2005</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, April 2, 2005</p><p>ORD C33594 Section 6</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.070.030">Section 17F.070.030</a> Abandoned Defined<br />
        <p>"Abandoned," in reference to property, means unattended and open and unsecured so that a person may gain admittance without damaging any portion of the property, or giving indications that no one is presently in possession, such as by disconnection of utilities, accumulation of debris, uncleanliness, disrepair, and other circumstances. Such properties are subject to the annual hearing processing fee as set out in <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=08.02.067">SMC 8.02.067</a>.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 15, 2010</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, April 21, 2010</p><p>ORD C34577 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.070.040">Section 17F.070.040</a> Boarded-up Building Defined<br />
        <p>A "boarded-up building" is a building any exterior opening of which is closed by any extrinsic device or in any manner designed or calculated to be permanent and which gives to the building the appearance of nonoccupancy or nonuse for an indefinite period of time. After one year a boarded-up building becomes an unfit building as provided in <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=17F.070.410">SMC 17F.070.410</a>.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, July 18, 2005</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, August 20, 2005</p><p>ORD C33687 Section 3</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.070.050">Section 17F.070.050</a> Ceiling Height Defined<br />
        <p>"Ceiling height" is the clear vertical distance from the finished floor to the finished ceiling above.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 28, 2005</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, April 2, 2005</p><p>ORD C33594 Section 6</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.070.060">Section 17F.070.060</a> Common Hallway Defined<br />
        <p>"Common hallway" is a hallway, corridor, passageway, vestibule, stairway, landing or platform in an apartment house, apartment hotel, boarding house, hotel, lodging house or rooming house, except those within an apartment, guestroom or suite of rooms.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 28, 2005</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, April 2, 2005</p><p>ORD C33594 Section 6</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.070.070">Section 17F.070.070</a> REPEALED (Efficiency Dwelling Unit Defined)<br />
        <p>
        	Repealed by ORD C35389<o:p></o:p></p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, May 23, 2016</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, June 30, 2016</p><p>ORD C35389 Section 11</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.070.080">Section 17F.070.080</a> Hot Water Defined<br />
        <p>"Hot water" is water at a temperature exceeding or equal to one hundred degrees Fahrenheit (Reference Washington State Amendment to the UPC).</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 7, 2010</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, July 1, 2010</p><p>ORD C34600 Section 7</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.070.090">Section 17F.070.090</a> Housekeeping Room Defined<br />
        <p>A "housekeeping room" is a single unit providing complete independent living facilities, including provisions for sleeping, eating and cooking, with a minimum floor area of one hundred twenty square feet.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 28, 2005</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, April 2, 2005</p><p>ORD C33594 Section 6</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.070.100">Section 17F.070.100</a> Kitchen Defined<br />
        <p>"Kitchen" is any room used, intended, or designed to be used for the preparation of food, and contains a sink, cooking facility, and a refrigerator.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 7, 2010</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, July 1, 2010</p><p>ORD C34600 Section 8</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.070.110">Section 17F.070.110</a> Residential Building Defined<br />
        <p>As used in this chapter "residential building" is either a dwelling, an apartment house, a lodging house or a hotel.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 28, 2005</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, April 2, 2005</p><p>ORD C33594 Section 6</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.070.120">Section 17F.070.120</a> Room Defined<br />
        <p>"Room" is an unsubdivided portion of the interior of a building.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 28, 2005</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, April 2, 2005</p><p>ORD C33594 Section 6</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.070.130">Section 17F.070.130</a> Substandard Building Defined<br />
        <p>A "substandard building" is a building which fails to meet the minimum standards of this chapter. In the generic sense the term includes "substandard buildings" and "unfit buildings" and "boarded-up buildings" as these terms are more fully defined and described herein.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 28, 2005</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, April 2, 2005</p><p>ORD C33594 Section 6</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.070.140">Section 17F.070.140</a> Superficial Floor Area Defined<br />
        <p>"Superficial floor area" is clear floor space, exclusive of fixed or built-in cabinets and appliances.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 28, 2005</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, April 2, 2005</p><p>ORD C33594 Section 6</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.070.150">Section 17F.070.150</a> Vent Shaft Defined<br />
        <p>A "vent shaft" is a court used only to ventilate a water closet, bath, toilet, kitchen, utility room or other service room.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 28, 2005</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, April 2, 2005</p><p>ORD C33594 Section 6</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.070.160">Section 17F.070.160</a> Window Defined<br />
        <p>"Window" is a glazed opening, including a glazed door, which opens upon a yard, court or vent shaft open and unobstructed to the sky.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 28, 2005</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, April 2, 2005</p><p>ORD C33594 Section 6</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.070.170">Section 17F.070.170</a> Construction – Structural Requirements<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">IBC Table 503 and Section 602 apply to all existing buildings except that:</span></span></span></span></p>
        
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">any type of construction permitted by the building code is allowed to continue, so long as:</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">foundations, floors, walls, roofs, and other structural components are capable of resisting all forces and loads;</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">the building is weather protected so as to shelter the occupants against the elements and to exclude dampness; and</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">wood is protected against termite damage and decay as provided in the building code;</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">every hotel and apartment house over two stories in height, regardless of capacity, must have an approved fire alarm system.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 7, 2010</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, July 1, 2010</p><p>ORD C34600 Section 9</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.070.180">Section 17F.070.180</a> Exit Requirements<br />
        <p>The exit requirements of the building code and the fire code are fully applicable to all existing buildings and portions of buildings. In addition the following sections, <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=17F.070.190">SMC 17F.070.190</a> through <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=17F.070.240">17F.070.240</a> apply to existing hotel and apartment buildings over two stories in height.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 28, 2005</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, April 2, 2005</p><p>ORD C33594 Section 6</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.070.190">Section 17F.070.190</a> REPEALED (Number of Exits)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C35349 Section 1<?xml:namespace prefix = o ns = "urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office" /><o:p></o:p></p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, January 11, 2016</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, February 24, 2016</p><p>ORD C35349 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.070.200">Section 17F.070.200</a> Interior Stairways<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Every interior stairway must be enclosed with walls of at least one-hour fire-resistive construction, except that where existing partitions form part of a stairwell enclosure, wood lath and plaster in good condition is an acceptable substitute.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Enclosure must include landings between flights and all corridors, passageways and public rooms necessary for continuous exit to the outside.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Doorways to required enclosures must be protected by a self-closing door equivalent to a solid wood door at least one and three-quarters inch thick with a two-inch nominal wood frame and rabbeted jamb.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="4" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">A stairway need not be enclosed, subject to approval:</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">in a continuous shaft if cut off at each story by fire-resistive construction as is required for stairwell enclosure; or</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">when the building has an approved automatic fire extinguishing system with sprinkler heads centered on both sides of every door entering an exit.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 28, 2005</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, April 2, 2005</p><p>ORD C33594 Section 6</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.070.210">Section 17F.070.210</a> Dead-end Corridors<br />
        <p>A dead-end corridor exceeding thirty-five feet in length may be approved if such corridor and adjoining areas where fire may endanger safe passage to an approved exit are protected by an approved automatic sprinkler system.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 28, 2005</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, April 2, 2005</p><p>ORD C33594 Section 6</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.070.220">Section 17F.070.220</a> Doors and Openings<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The requirements of IBC Sections 1014, 1015, 1016, 1017, 1018, 1019, and 1020 apply, except that:</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">an existing, solid, bonded wood core door, one and three-eighths inch thick, or an equivalent, may be kept; and</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">a door or other opening protected on both sides by an approved thermal detection or sprinkler system may open on an exit, so long as the opening does not lead to a special area to be protected, as defined in <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=17F.080.090"><span style="color:blue">SMC 17F.080.090</span></a>.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Transoms and openings (except doors from corridors to rooms) must be fixed closed and covered with material equivalent to the surrounding separation.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">A door, when open, must not reduce the minimum required width of an exit way more than seven inches.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 7, 2010</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, July 1, 2010</p><p>ORD C34600 Section 11</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.070.230">Section 17F.070.230</a> Exterior Stairways<br />
        <p>Exterior stairways must be noncombustible; however, wood stairways of at least two-inch nominal thickness may be used on three-story buildings in approved locations and maintained in a safe condition.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 28, 2005</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, April 2, 2005</p><p>ORD C33594 Section 6</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.070.240">Section 17F.070.240</a> Fire Escapes<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">An existing fire escape may be used as one means of exit, subject to approval, if:</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">maintained in a safe condition;</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">the pitch does not exceed sixty degrees;</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">the width is at least eighteen inches;</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="4">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">the treads are at least four inches wide;</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="5">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">it extends to the ground or has counterbalanced stairs which reach the ground.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">An opening giving access must have a minimum net clear opening of nine square feet, the smallest dimension being at least twenty-nine inches.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">A window giving egress or rescue must have a finished sill height of no more than thirty-six inches above the floor.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 28, 2005</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, April 2, 2005</p><p>ORD C33594 Section 6</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.070.250">Section 17F.070.250</a> Light and Ventilation Requirements<br />
        <p>
        	IBC subsection 1203.5 provides for natural ventilation and subsection 1205 applies to all existing buildings except that the building official may approve artificial light, in lieu of natural light, in guestrooms, dormitories, and other habitable rooms.</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, May 23, 2016</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, June 30, 2016</p><p>ORD C35389 Section 12</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.070.260">Section 17F.070.260</a> Sanitation Requirements<br />
        <p>
        	In addition to IBC subsection 2902.1 and Washington State Amendments Table 2902.1:</p>
        <ol type="A">
        	<li>
        		<p>
        			splash backs and drain boards must have an impervious surface;</p>
        	</li>
        	<li>
        		<p>
        			every plumbing fixture must be connected to either a public sanitary sewer system or an approved private sewage disposal system;</p>
        	</li>
        	<li>
        		<p>
        			all plumbing fixtures must be connected to an approved water supply system and must be provided with hot and cold water, except that water closets need have only cold water;</p>
        	</li>
        	<li>
        		<p>
        			all plumbing fixtures must be of glazed earthenware or other similar approved nonabsorbent material and must be installed in accordance with the plumbing code;</p>
        	</li>
        	<li>
        		<p>
        			all sanitary facilities must be installed and maintained in a safe and sanitary condition.</p>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, May 23, 2016</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, June 30, 2016</p><p>ORD C35389 Section 13</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.070.270">Section 17F.070.270</a> REPEALED (Yards and Courts)<br />
        <p>
        	Repealed by ORD C35389<o:p></o:p></p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, May 23, 2016</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, June 30, 2016</p><p>ORD C35389 Section 14</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.070.280">Section 17F.070.280</a> Room Dimensions<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">IBC subsection 1208.2 is modified so that the minimum required ceiling height is seven feet.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">IBC subsection 1208.3 Room Area.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Every room used for both cooking and living, or both living and sleeping, purposes must have at least one hundred fifty square feet of superficial floor area; and</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Every room used for sleeping purposes by more than two persons must have an additional fifty square feet of superficial floor area for each occupant in excess of two.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 7, 2010</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, July 1, 2010</p><p>ORD C34600 Section 15</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.070.290">Section 17F.070.290</a> Housekeeping Rooms<br />
        <p>A housekeeping room is permitted under this chapter if it has a sink with hot and cold running water and sufficient storage areas for clothing and cooking purposes. Only a nonportable electric range is permitted. Such range may be used for cooking only and it must be located so as to avoid contact with combustible materials.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 28, 2005</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, April 2, 2005</p><p>ORD C33594 Section 6</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.070.300">Section 17F.070.300</a> Fire Alarm Systems<br />
        <p>
        	Every existing apartment and hotel building over two stories in height must have an approved Type 2A alarm system, as provided in IFC Section Chart # 907, and such system must be maintained as provided in <a href="https://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=17F.080.250" target="_blank">SMC 17F.080.250</a>.</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, May 23, 2016</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, June 30, 2016</p><p>ORD C35389 Section 15</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.070.310">Section 17F.070.310</a> Heating Requirements<br />
        <p>In addition to IBC section 1204:</p>
        <ol type="A">
        <li>no unvented or open flame gas heater is permitted as the primary source of heating; and<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>all heating devices and appliances must be of an approved type and installed and maintained in a safe manner and condition. </li></ol>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 7, 2010</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, July 1, 2010</p><p>ORD C34600 Section 16</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.070.320">Section 17F.070.320</a> Ventilation<br />
        <p>
        <ol type="A">
        <li>Ventilating equipment must be approved as to type, installation and maintenance.<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>Wherever mechanical ventilation is employed in lieu of natural ventilation, such mechanical system must be in operation during occupancy.<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>The ventilation of rooms and areas containing fuel-burning appliances must be adequate for proper combustion. </li></ol>
        <p></p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 28, 2005</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, April 2, 2005</p><p>ORD C33594 Section 6</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.070.330">Section 17F.070.330</a> Separation of Occupancies<br />
        <p>The occupancy separation requirements of the building code apply to hotel and apartment buildings over two stories in height.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 28, 2005</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, April 2, 2005</p><p>ORD C33594 Section 6</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.070.340">Section 17F.070.340</a> Electrical Requirements<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Electrical equipment, wiring and appliances of an approved type which were installed and have been maintained in a safe manner need not be replaced. An installation which was improperly installed or which has been damaged or deteriorated to the point of hazard must be replaced, repaired, or altered to meet current loads in accordance with the electrical code.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Every dwelling unit in an apartment house must have a separate circuit for:</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">general lighting;</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">the dryer;</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">the electric range;</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="4">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">the furnace;</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="5">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">the hot water tank; and</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="6">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">the kitchen.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Every efficiency dwelling unit must have a separate circuit for:</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">the kitchen area;</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">the living area; and</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">the range.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="4" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Every housekeeping room must have a separate circuit for:</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">general lighting; and</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">the electric range, if required.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="5" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">There shall be at least one supplied electric light fixture in every:</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">bathroom and water closet compartment;</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">furnace room;</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">common hallway; and</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="4">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">laundry room.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="6" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Duplex outlets are required as follows:</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Dwelling unit:</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Kitchen: two;</span></span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="2" style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Living room: two;</span></span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="3" style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Bathroom: one, which may be in a wall lighting fixture;</span></span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="4" style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Other habitable room: two, on opposite walls.</span></span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Efficiency dwelling unit: four, two in kitchen area;</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Housekeeping room: three.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 28, 2005</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, April 2, 2005</p><p>ORD C33594 Section 6</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.070.350">Section 17F.070.350</a> Modular Homes<br />
        <p>Every modular home must comply with the state regulations in effect at the time of its construction and occupancy. If there were no state regulations at the time, a modular home must comply with this title.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 28, 2005</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, April 2, 2005</p><p>ORD C33594 Section 6</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.070.360">Section 17F.070.360</a> REPEALED (Stair Construction)<br />
        <p>
        	Repealed by ORD C35389<o:p></o:p></p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, May 23, 2016</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, June 30, 2016</p><p>ORD C35389 Section 16</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.070.370">Section 17F.070.370</a> Allocation of Responsibility<br />
        <p>
        <ol type="A">
        <li><a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=17F.070.370">SMC 17F.070.370</a> through <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=17F.070.390">17F.070.390</a> are intended to specify who has the primary maintenance responsibility for residential buildings whenever the owner(s) and the occupant(s) are different persons.<br />&nbsp; 
        <li>The allocation of maintenance responsibility provided in this chapter is subject to the general laws of the state, including specifically the Landlord-Tenant Acts (chapters 59.18 and 59.20 RCW). This chapter does not derogate the rights of contract or affect the principle that the owner of property is ultimately responsible for its condition and use. </li></ol>
        <p></p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 28, 2005</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, April 2, 2005</p><p>ORD C33594 Section 6</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.070.380">Section 17F.070.380</a> Responsibilities of Owners<br />
        <p>The responsibilities of an owner under this chapter include:</p>
        <ol type="A">
        <li>maintaining the building in a sound structural condition;<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>keeping those parts of the premises under his control, including shared, common or public areas, clean, safe and sanitary;<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>furnishing required sanitary facilities;<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>furnishing and maintaining devices, equipment, or facilities for the prevention of insect and rodent infestation;<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>exterminating insects or rodents upon infestation, when not clearly the obligation of the occupant. </li></ol>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 28, 2005</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, April 2, 2005</p><p>ORD C33594 Section 6</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.070.390">Section 17F.070.390</a> Responsibilities of Occupants<br />
        <p>The responsibilities of an occupant under this chapter include:</p>
        <ol type="A">
        <li>keeping those parts of the premises under his control clean, safe and sanitary;<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>keeping plumbing and other fixtures clean and sanitary and using reasonable care in their proper use and operation;<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>preventing infestation and exterminating insects and rodents when only his part of the premises is infested and the rest of the building is reasonably protected against such infestation;<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>disposing of garbage and refuse in proper receptacles, and providing such receptacles when the owner does not;<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>refraining from placing or accumulating material and otherwise preventing the creation of a fire, health, or safety hazard to the occupants of the building;<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>preventing any use of his part of the premises in any manner violative of law. </li></ol>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 28, 2005</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, April 2, 2005</p><p>ORD C33594 Section 6</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.070.400">Section 17F.070.400</a> Substandard Buildings<br />
        <p>In determining whether a building is a substandard or unfit for human habitation so as to require its owner to repair and rehabilitate the building, the building official and the hearing examiner consider the number and extent of the following factors: </p>
        <ol type="A">
        <li>Dilapidation:&nbsp; Exterior decay, water damage.<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>Structural defects:&nbsp; Foundation, wall and roof framing.<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>Unsanitary conditions:&nbsp; Waste accumulation, health hazards.<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>Defective/inoperable plumbing.<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>Inadequate weatherproofing: Siding, roofing and glazing.<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>No activated utility service for one year.<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>Inoperable or inadequate heating system.<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>Hazardous electrical conditions.<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>Structure has been boarded more than one year and no approved rehabilitation plan.<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>Structure used in the manufacture of methamphetamine or any other illegal drugs and has been condemned by the Spokane county health district and the owner has failed to abate the nuisance condition.<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>Fire-damaged structure.<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>Defects increasing the hazards of fire, accident or other calamity.</li></ol>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 12, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Monday, March 12, 2007</p><p>ORD C33989 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.070.410">Section 17F.070.410</a> Unfit Buildings<br />
        <p>The building official or hearing examiner may determine that the building/structure is unfit for human habitation and orders demolition if any of the substandard conditions listed in <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=17F.070.400">SMC 17F.070.400</a> are found to exist to such an extent as to be dangerous or injurious to the health or safety of the buildings occupants or community.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, July 18, 2005</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, August 20, 2005</p><p>ORD C33687 Section 5</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.070.420">Section 17F.070.420</a> Complaint – Content<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Whenever the building inspector, upon inspection and any other investigation as may be done, finds a building or premises to be in violation of this chapter, he prepares a written complaint:</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">specifying the violations; and</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">stating his determination that the property is a boarded-up building, substandard building, unfit building, or otherwise a public nuisance; and</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">giving notice of a hearing before the Building Official at a time and place stated; and</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="4">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">advising that any interested person may file an answer to the complaint and appear and be heard at the hearing; and</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="5">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">advising that a copy of the complaint will be filed of record in the office of the Spokane County Auditor.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Whenever the building inspector and fire inspector, upon investigation, find a building or portion to be in violation of the requirements of this chapter for apartment and hotel buildings over two stories in height, they prepare an inspection report:</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">containing a detailed list of deficiencies, including citations to the appropriate code or regulation sections;</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">giving a timetable for correction; and</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">requiring a written response or notice of appeal within thirty days.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 20, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Friday, November 28, 2025</p><p>ORD C36753 Section 36</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.070.430">Section 17F.070.430</a> Complaint – Service<br />
        <p>The complaint and the report of inspection under <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=17F.070.420">SMC 17F.070.420</a> are served as provided in <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=17F.010.050">SMC 17F.010.050(A)</a>.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 28, 2005</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, April 2, 2005</p><p>ORD C33594 Section 6</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.070.440">Section 17F.070.440</a> Building Official Hearing<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Unless arrangements satisfactory to the Building Official are made for the repair, vacation, demolition, or other necessary disposition of the property prior to the time fixed in the complaint under&nbsp;</span></span></span><a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=17F.070.420" style="color:blue; text-decoration:underline"><span style="background-color:white">SMC 17F.070.420(A)</span></a><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">&nbsp;for the hearing, the Building Official holds a hearing. Based on the complaint, any answer to the complaint and any evidence presented, the Building Official:</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">determines whether the building is boarded up, substandard, unfit, abandoned, or otherwise a nuisance and subject to an annual hearing processing fee. This fee may be assessed annually after a hearing to determine if the building remains as a boarded up, substandard, unfit, abandoned, or nuisance. The Building Official may also assess the annual monitoring fee if the building is abandoned, unsecured, or otherwise a nuisance;</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">determines what action must be taken by the owner (such as repair and rehabilitation, vacation, demolition) to render the property in compliance with this chapter; and</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">after the hearing, prepares in writing findings in support of their determinations and an order directing the owner to take specified corrective action within a specified time.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">An interested person may appeal an inspection report regarding apartment and hotel buildings over two stories in height under&nbsp;</span></span></span><a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=17F.070.420" style="color:blue; text-decoration:underline"><span style="background-color:white">SMC 17F.070.420(B)</span></a><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">&nbsp;to the Building Official and fire official by filing, within thirty days of service, with the Building Official a written notice of appeal, specifying the provisions appealed from and the grounds of the appeal. If an appeal is filed, the Building Official and fire official set a time and place for hearing, within fifteen days unless otherwise agreed to, and advise the appellant by any appropriate means. Based on the evidence at the hearing the Building Official and the fire official may:</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol style="margin-left:40px">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">affirm or reverse the findings or rulings in the inspection report;</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="margin-left:40px">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">grant a variance; or</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="margin-left:40px">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">make some adjustment of the required corrective action or the time for corrective action, imposing such conditions as necessary to assure reasonable safety.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 20, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Friday, November 28, 2025</p><p>ORD C36753 Section 37</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.070.450">Section 17F.070.450</a> Effect of Hearing Order<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">The order made at the hearing before the Building Official under&nbsp;</span></span></span><a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=17F.070.440" style="color:blue; text-decoration:underline"><span style="background-color:white">SMC 17F.070.440(A)</span></a><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">&nbsp;and the order upon the appeal hearing before the Building Official and fire official under&nbsp;</span></span></span><a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=17F.070.440" style="color:blue; text-decoration:underline"><span style="background-color:white">SMC 17F.070.440(B)</span></a><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">, and the notice of right of appeal, are served upon the parties in the manner provided in&nbsp;</span></span></span><a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=17F.010.050" style="color:blue; text-decoration:underline"><span style="background-color:white">SMC 17F.010.050</span></a><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">If no appeal be filed from the order of the Building Official within the time allowed, the Development Services Department files a certified copy of the order with the Spokane County Auditor as a supplement to the lis pendens previously filed. Thereafter such final order serves as a basis for any further judicial or administrative action, including the assessment against the property of any costs and expenses of the City in taking action to effect the order and bring the property into compliance.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 20, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Friday, November 28, 2025</p><p>ORD C36753 Section 38</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.070.460">Section 17F.070.460</a> Appeal<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">An interested party may appeal an order made under <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=17F.070.440"><span style="color:blue">SMC 17F.070.440</span></a>:</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">to the hearing examiner concerning a boarded-up, substandard or unfit building; or</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">to the hearing officer provided in <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=04.06.070"><span style="color:blue">SMC 4.06.070</span></a>, concerning technical code issues respecting an apartment or hotel building over two stories in height; or</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">to the city council concerning an apartment or hotel building over two stories in height.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The hearing examiner, upon the hearing, either affirms, vacates or modifies the director&rsquo;s order or continues the hearing. The examiner does not continue a hearing beyond sixty days after the appeal is filed without the consent of the appellant. Should the examiner fail to decide the appeal within the sixty-day period (or within such longer period as the appellant may agree to), the order of the director becomes the final order and the appellant may seek judicial review of the director&rsquo;s order.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The director causes the final order resulting from the hearing examiner&rsquo;s hearing to be served and filed in the manner provided in <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=17F.070.450"><span style="color:blue">SMC 17F.070.450(B)</span></a> and takes all other appropriate action to enforce the order.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="4" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The city council hearing an appeal determines whether the director of building and fire official acted in accordance with the terms and in a manner so as to effectuate the life safety purposes of this code and either affirms the order or remands for further hearing.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 28, 2005</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, April 2, 2005</p><p>ORD C33594 Section 6</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.070.470">Section 17F.070.470</a> Compliance with Order<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The order under this chapter specifies the action to be taken by the owner and establishes a time or timeframe for compliance.&nbsp; </span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">So long as a building is boarded up, or unfit, substandard, or abandoned and subject to the building official hearing process, the owner must pay an annual fee as provided in</span></span><a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=08.02.067"> </a><a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=08.02.067"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">SMC 8.02.067</span></span></a><a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=08.02.067"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">.</span></span></a><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"> This fee is lienable under</span></span><a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=17F.070.500"> </a><a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=17F.070.500"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">SMC 17F.070.500</span></span></a><a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=17F.070.500"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">.</span></span></a><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"> Otherwise, the owner must cause the building to be occupied in compliance with all applicable code requirements. However, it is the intent of this chapter that boarding a dangerous building is a temporary solution to imminent danger and a building may not remain boarded up longer than two years unless an extension of time is part of a plan approved by the building official or hearing examiner detailing the future rehabilitation, sale, demolition, or other disposition of the building. </span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">A property remaining boarded up longer than two years may be subject to demolition by order of the building official. </span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The building official shall order the owner of any premises upon which is located any structure, which in the building official&rsquo;s judgment is so dilapidated or has become so out of repair as to be dangerous, unsafe, unsanitary, or otherwise unfit for human habitation or occupancy, and that it is unreasonable to repair the structure, to demolish and remove such structure; or if such structure is capable of being made safe by repairs, to repair and make safe and sanitary or to demolish and remove at the owner&rsquo;s option; or where there has been a cessation of normal construction of any structure for a period of more than two years, to demolish and remove such structure. (2006 International Property Maintenance Code section 110.1).&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">When the building is of sufficient value to be repairable, the building official may recommend action by the City to obtain the property through eminent domain, pursuant to the provisions of the chapter 35.80A Revised Code of Washington. </span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="4">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">As an alternative to demolition, when appropriate, the building official may issue an order to refer substandard, abandoned, unfit, or nuisance properties to Superior Court in pursuit of a receivership order.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The owner of a substandard building must repair and rehabilitate it so as to bring it into compliance with the standards of this chapter, at a minimum, or into compliance with the new work and replacement requirements of the building and associated codes provided in</span></span><a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Title=17F"> </a><a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Title=17F"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">chapters </span></span></a><a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Title=17F"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">17F.030 through 17F.060 SMC</span></span></a><a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Title=17F"> </a><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">and</span></span><a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Title=17F"> </a><a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Title=17F"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">chapters 17F.080 through 17F.100 </span></span></a><a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Title=17F"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">SMC</span></span></a><a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Title=17F"> </a><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">if applicable by their terms. When warranted by the nature and extent of the repairs and the type of occupancy, the order may require the building to be vacated and secured during rehabilitation. </span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="4" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The owner of an unfit building must cause it to be vacated, secured against entry, demolished, and the land filled and cleared. When warranted by the location of the building and the nature of the defects the order may allow demolition to be delayed upon such conditions, such as clearing and securing, as will safeguard health and safety. </span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="5" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Should the owner of an unfit building propose a written undertaking, acceptable to the building official or the hearing examiner, giving assurance and security that the building can be safely rehabilitated in a reasonable time, then the order can direct rehabilitation according to the undertaking, in lieu of demolition. Upon the owner&rsquo;s failure to accomplish his undertaking, the building official or hearing examiner may summarily order demolition or receivership, or when the building is of sufficient value to be repairable, the building official may recommend action by the City to obtain the property through eminent domain, pursuant to the provisions of chapter 35.80A Revised Code of Washington. </span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="6" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">An order respecting a building under this chapter may require the owner to take specified action in regard to the surrounding ground whereby nuisance, such as dry vegetation or other combustible accumulations, or toxic, septic, or unsafe substances, is abated. </span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 1, 2021</p><p>Effective Date: Friday, March 12, 2021</p><p>ORD C36004 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.070.480">Section 17F.070.480</a> Administrative Responsibilities<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The director is the building official or a designated employee.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The director has the responsibility, jointly with the fire official as to some functions relating to the structural and fire containment requirements of hotels and apartments having more than two stories, to:</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">inspect and investigate all buildings and premises for compliance with the existing building and conservation code;</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">review and approve plans and specifications for building permits;</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">make and promulgate rules, regulations and interpretations;</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="4">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">initiate proceedings, including the preparation, service and posting of complaints and notices, and including prosecutions, to enforce the existing building and conservation code;</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="5">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">process, conduct and hear departmental appeals;</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="6">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">process appeals to the appropriate hearing officer or to the city council;</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="7">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">keep records of all inspections, proceedings and other administrative activities;</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="8">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">provide technical and clerical assistance to the construction review board as provided in <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Chapter=04.06"><span style="color:blue">chapter 4.06 SMC</span></a> and the hearing examiner.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The fire official has responsibility, along with the director, with respect to hotels and apartments having more than two stories, in regard to:</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">approving fire warning systems;</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">making rules, regulations and interpretations for structural and fire containment requirements;</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">inspection and serving of reports and notices;</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="4">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">hearing appeals from departmental decisions;</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="5">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">processing appeals to the appropriate appeal board or to the city council;</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="6">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">approving building permits and plans.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="4" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The hearing officer pursuant to <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=04.06.070"><span style="color:blue">SMC 4.06.070</span></a> determines appeals from rulings of the director and fire official which are of a technical nature.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="5" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The hearing examiner, with respect to unfit and substandard buildings:</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">reviews and hears appeals from proceedings and orders of the director, not of a technical nature;</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">makes rules and regulations;</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">recommends procedures and legislation.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="6" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Except for those matters of a technical nature which are appealed to the hearing officer under <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=04.06.070"><span style="color:blue">SMC 4.06.070</span></a>, the city council hears appeals from rulings of the director and fire official regarding hotels and apartments having more than two stories.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 28, 2005</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, April 2, 2005</p><p>ORD C33594 Section 6</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.070.490">Section 17F.070.490</a> Enforcement<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Whenever an owner has failed to complete the action required by an order under this chapter: </span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">the building official or the hearing examiner may extend the time for completion, imposing such conditions as may seem warranted, if the owner has made substantial progress; or </span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">the director causes the ordered action to be done, by competitive bid contract whenever feasible, or by negotiated contract, or by city forces when circumstances do not allow time for bidding. </span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">All work of rehabilitation and demolition done pursuant to an order made under this chapter is subject to all applicable laws respecting permits, contractor registration and certification of workers, except work done by city forces under emergency circumstances. </span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Invitations to bid on a demolition contract shall provide that salvage be awarded to the contractor as a credit against the contract price. A bid based on an estimate of the value of salvage may not be changed to reflect actual salvage value. The director may invite and receive bids before the time for compliance by the owner has expired. </span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="4" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="margin-left: 0in; margin-right: 0in; text-align: justify;"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">As an alternative to demolition, when appropriate, the building official may issue an order to refer substandard, abandoned, unfit, or nuisance properties to Superior Court in pursuit of a receivership order.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 1, 2021</p><p>Effective Date: Friday, March 12, 2021</p><p>ORD C36004 Section 2</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.070.500">Section 17F.070.500</a> Lien for Costs<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">As provided in RCW 35.80.030(1)(h), all costs to the City of repairs, alterations, or improvements; or vacating and closing; or removal or demolition are a lien against the property, to the maximum extent permitted by law. Lien costs includes costs of administration of the above listed items, including maintenance and monitoring ordered by the building official or his designee of any dwelling, building, or structure. Lien costs further include:</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">the amount of relocation assistance payments that a property owner has not repaid to a municipality or other local government entity that has advanced relocation assistance payments to tenants under RCW 59.18.085, and</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">all penalties and interest that accrue as a result of the failure of the property owner to timely repay the amount of these relocation assistance payments under RCW 59.18.085.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Such fees shall be certified by the City treasurer to the County treasurer, and are a charge and lien against the property and are, unless sooner paid and discharged, collected as property taxes as provided by law.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 15, 2010</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, April 21, 2010</p><p>ORD C34577 Section 4</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.070.510">Section 17F.070.510</a> Emergency Action<br />
        <p>This chapter does not impair or affect the ability of the building official or fire official to take whatever summary action is required to protect the public health and safety in the exercise of the police power.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 28, 2005</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, April 2, 2005</p><p>ORD C33594 Section 6</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.070.520">Section 17F.070.520</a> REPEALED (Foreclosure Registration Program)<br />
        <p>REPEALED&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, July 14, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, August 20, 2025</p><p>ORD C36701 Section 6</p>				<p><a href="/smc/?Chapter=17F.080">Chapter 17F.080</a> Fire Code</p>
        					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.080.010">Section 17F.080.010</a> Adoption of International Fire Code<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">The Washington State current amended edition of the International Fire Code (IFC) and related standards, published by the International Code Council, as modified by this title, is the fire code of the City of Spokane except as otherwise provided.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">The following amendments are made to the International Fire Code:</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol style="margin-left:40px">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Section 101.1 is modified to read as follows:</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Title.</span></span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:120px; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">These regulations shall be known as the fire code of the City of Spokane, hereinafter referred to as &ldquo;this code.&rdquo;</span></span></span></span></p>
        
        <ol start="2" style="margin-left:40px">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Section 112.4 is modified to read as follows:</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Violation Penalties.</span></span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:120px; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Persons who shall violate a provision of this code or shall fail to comply with any of the requirements, thereof, or who shall erect, install, alter, repair, or do work in violation of the approved construction documents or directive of the fire code official or of a permit or certificate used under provisions of this code shall be subject to a Class I Civil Infraction or the provisions of chapter 1.05 SMC. Each day that a violation continues after due notice has been served shall be deemed a separate offense.</span></span></span></span></p>
        
        <ol start="3" style="margin-left:40px">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Section 113.4 is modified to read as follows:</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Failure to Comply.</span></span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:120px; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Any person who shall continue any work after having been served with a stop work order, except such work as that person is directed to perform to remove a violation or unsafe condition, shall be subject to a Class one civil infraction or penalties identified in chapter 1.05 SMC.</span></span></span></span></p>
        
        <ol start="4" style="margin-left:40px">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">IFC Sections 503.1, 503.1.2, 503.1.3, 503.2, 503.3, and 503.4 are adopted as published. <span style="background-color:white">Section 503.1.1 is adopted and revised as follows:</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:80px; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><strong><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">503.1.1 Buildings and facilities.&nbsp;</span></span></strong><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Approved<em>&nbsp;</em>fire apparatus access roads shall be provided for every facility, building or portion of a building hereafter constructed or moved into or within the jurisdiction<u> </u>prior to the delivery of combustible construction materials to the site. The fire apparatus access road shall comply with the requirements of this section and shall extend to within 200 feet (60 960 mm) of all portions of the facility and all portions of the&nbsp;<em>exterior walls&nbsp;</em>of the first story of the building as measured by an&nbsp;<em>approved&nbsp;</em>route around the exterior of the building or&nbsp;facility.</span></span></span></span></p>
        
        <p style="margin-left:80px; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><strong><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Exceptions:</span></span></strong></span></span></p>
        
        <ol style="margin-left:40px">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">For buildings equipped throughout with an approved automatic sprinkler system<em>&nbsp;</em>installed in accordance with Section 903.3.1.1, 903.3.1.2 or 903.3.1.3 the distance shall extend to 240 feet.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="margin-left:40px">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Fire apparatus access roads cannot be installed because of location on property, topography, waterways, nonnegotiable grades or other similar conditions, and an approved<em>&nbsp;</em>alternative means of fire protection is provided.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="margin-left:40px">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">There are not more than two Group R-3, IRC, or Group U occupancies.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="4" style="margin-left:40px">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Where approved by the <em>fire code official</em>, fire apparatus access roads shall be permitted to be exempted or modified for:</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Solar photovoltaic power generation facilities.</span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="2" style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Additions of 200 square feet or less to existing non-conforming residential code buildings.</span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="5" style="margin-left:40px">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Chapter 56 is amended with chapter 10.33A SMC.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="6" style="margin-left:40px">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Section 903.2.11.5 is revised to read:</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:80px; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">A wet chemical suppression system shall be installed in a commercial kitchen exhaust hood and duct system to meet the compliance of Section 904.</span></span></span></span></p>
        
        <ol start="7" style="margin-left:40px">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Section 904.2.2 is revised to read:</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:80px; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Each required commercial kitchen exhaust hood and duct system required by Section 609 to have a Type 1 hood shall be protected with a wet chemical suppression system installed in accordance with this code.</span></span></span></span></p>
        
        <ol start="8" style="margin-left:40px">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Section 904.13.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:80px; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Replace the first paragraph and the five types to read:</span></span></span></span></p>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol style="list-style-type:lower-alpha; margin-left:40px">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">904.13 &ndash; Commercial Cooking Systems.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:120px; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">The automatic fire extinguishing system for commercial cooking systems shall be a wet-chemical type system. The wet-chemical system shall be tested in accordance with UL 300 and listed and labeled for the intended application. The system shall be installed in accordance with this code, its listing, and the manufacturer&rsquo;s installation instructions. Wet-chemical extinguishing systems shall be installed in accordance with NFPA 17A.</span></span></span></span></p>
        
        <ol start="9" style="margin-left:40px">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Section 904.13 &ndash; Exception; Section 904.12 Items 1, 2, 3, 4, and 5;</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:80px; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Section 904.13.3; Section 904.13.4 are not adopted.</span></span></span></span></p>
        
        <ol start="10" style="margin-left:40px">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Section 905.1 &ndash; Add the following to end of the paragraph:</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:80px; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Class II and Class III standpipes are not allowed for new standpipes in the City of Spokane. All requirements for Class II and Class III shall be Class I and references to one- and one-half inch outlets shall be changed to two and one-half inches. There are no requirements for two and one-half inch hose to be provided (i.e., stages).</span></span></span></span></p>
        
        <ol start="11" style="margin-left:40px">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Section 906.1.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:80px; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Add Exception to read as follows:</span></span></span></span></p>
        
        <ol start="11">
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol style="list-style-type:lower-alpha; margin-left:40px">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Portable fire extinguishers are not required for commercial residential buildings that do not have an interior or exterior common space.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="12" style="margin-left:40px">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Section 909.2.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:80px; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Revise the second sentence to read as follows:</span></span></span></span></p>
        
        <p style="margin-left:80px; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">The <em>construction documents </em>shall be prepared and stamped by a licensed engineer registered with the Spokane Fire Department and shall include sufficient information and detail to describe adequately the elements of the design necessary for the proper implementation of the smoke control systems.</span></span></span></span></p>
        
        <ol start="13" style="margin-left:40px">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Section 1011.14.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:80px; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Remove &ldquo;and for access to unoccupied roofs&rdquo; from last sentence.</span></span></span></span></p>
        
        <ol start="14" style="margin-left:40px">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Section 1011.12</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:80px; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Remove &ldquo;alternating tread device,&rdquo; from exception.</span></span></span></span></p>
        
        <ol start="15" style="margin-left:40px">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Section 1023.9.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:80px; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Revise the second sentence to read as follows:</span></span></span></span></p>
        
        <p style="margin-left:80px; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">&ldquo;. . . the story of, the number of floors above grade (if it is different from the story number), and the direction . . .&rdquo;</span></span></span></span></p>
        
        <ol start="16" style="margin-left:40px">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Section 5704.2.9.6.1 Modify to read:</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:80px; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">&ldquo;outside of buildings shall be in accordance with table 5705.3.4(2)</span></span></span></span></p>
        
        <ol start="17" style="margin-left:40px">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Section 5706.2.4.4 Modify to read:</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:80px; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Remove the last part of the last sentence after above-ground tanks and add: outside of buildings shall be in accordance with table 5705.3.4(2)</span></span></span></span></p>
        
        <ol start="18" style="margin-left:40px">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Section 5806.2 Modify:</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:80px; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Remove the last part of the last sentence after outside of buildings and add: shall be in accordance with the requirements of the Authority Having Jurisdiction.</span></span></span></span></p>
        
        <ol start="19" style="margin-left:40px">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Section 6104.2.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:80px; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Remove the last part of the last sentence: &ldquo;(Jurisdiction to specify)&rdquo;.</span></span> </span></span></p>
        
        <ol start="20" style="margin-left:40px">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Section 3307.1 Revise to read:</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:80px; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><strong><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">3307.1 Required access. </span></span></strong><em><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Approved </span></span></em><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">vehicle access for firefighting shall be provided to all construction or demolition sites prior to the delivery of combustible construction materials to the site or the commencement of demolition activities. Vehicle access shall be provided to within 100 feet (30 480 mm) of temporary or permanent fire department connections. Vehicle access shall be provided by permanent roads, capable of supporting vehicle loading under all weather conditions unless otherwise approved by the Fire Code Official.</span></span></span></span>&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p style="margin-left:80px; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 16, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, July 30, 2025</p><p>ORD C36695 Section 3</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.080.020">Section 17F.080.020</a> REPEALED (Adoption of National Fire Protection Association Standards)<br />
        <p>Repealed by ORD C34993.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 17, 2013</p><p>Effective Date: Monday, July 1, 2013</p><p>ORD C34993 Section 4</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17F.080.030">Section 17F.080.030</a> Appendices Adopted<br />
        <p style="margin-right:0in"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">The following appendices of the International Fire Code are adopted as part of the fire code of the City:</span></span></span></span></p>
        
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Appendix B - Fire-Flow Requirements for Buildings.</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Appendix C &ndash; Fire Hydrant Locations and Distribution.</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Table C102.1 &ndash; Revise the column for &lsquo;Maximum distance from any point on street or road frontage to a hydrant to be five hundred feet for each row.</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Table C102.1 &ndash; Footnote b is not adopted.</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Appendix D &ndash; Fire Apparatus Access Roads.</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:40px; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Provided, fire department access will be in conformance to Appendix D with the following exceptions:</span></span></span></span></span></p>
        
        <ol style="margin-left:40px">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">D103.3.</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:80px; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">The minimum external turning radius will be fifty feet and minimum internal turning radius will be twenty-eight feet.</span></span></span></span></span></p>
        
        <ol start="2" style="margin-left:40px">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Table D103.4.</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:80px; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">The cul-de-sac diameter shall be one hundred feet.</span></span></span></span></span></p>
        
        <ol start="3" style="margin-left:40px">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Figure D103.1.</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:80px; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">The ninety-six feet diameter cul-de-sac is revised to one hundred feet diameter.</span></span></span></span></span></p>
        
        <ol start="4" style="margin-left:40px">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">D103.5.</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:80px; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Revise/Add the following:</span></span></span></span></span></p>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">The minimum gate width shall be twenty feet unless reviewed and accepted by the fire official or designated representative (to be no less than fourteen feet).</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="2" style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">At least one gate off of public or private streets that is required for fire apparatus access onto a site shall be inset a minimum of 48&rsquo; from the edge of curb or curb line.</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="5" style="margin-left:40px">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><u><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">D103.6</span></span></u></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:80px; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Revise to read:</span></span></span></span></p>
        
        <p style="margin-left:80px; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Signs.&nbsp; Where required by the fire code official, fire apparatus access roads shall be marked with permanent &ldquo;NO PARKING-FIRE Lane&rdquo; signs complying with Figure D103.6.<u> The signs shall be spaced following City signage standards.&nbsp; </u>Signs shall have a minimum dimension of 12 inches (305 mm) wide by 18 inches (457 mm) high and have red letters on a white reflective background.&nbsp; Signs shall be posted on once or both sides of the fire apparatus road as required by Section D103.6.1 or D103.6.2.</span></span></span></span></p>
        
        <ol start="6" style="margin-left:40px">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">D103.7.1.</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:80px; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Residential Driveways. Driveways used as fire lanes for single family and two-family dwellings can be reduced to an unobstructed width of twelve feet wide as long as there is a code compliant fifty-foot radius turn-around or approved hammerhead within one hundred fifty feet of all points around the dwelling.</span></span></span></span></span></p>
        
        <ol start="7" style="margin-left:40px">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">D103.7.2.</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:80px; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Fire access roads can be designed in&nbsp;accordance with&nbsp;</span></span></span><span style="color:black"><a href="https://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=17H.010.140"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:#006699">SMC 17H.010.140</span></span></span></a></span><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">,&nbsp;Emergency Vehicle Access and Staging Areas, <u>can be used </u>as an approved alternative with the approval of the fire official for residential access roads.</span></span></span></span></span></p>
        
        <ol start="8" style="margin-left:40px">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><u><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">D105.1 </span></span></span></u></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:80px; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><u><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Revise the following:</span></span></span></u></span></span></p>
        
        <p style="margin-left:80px; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><u><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">D105.1.&nbsp; Where required.</span></span></span></u></span></span></p>
        
        <p style="margin-left:80px; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Where the vertical distance between lowest level of fire department vehicle access and the highest roof surface exceeds 30 feet (9144 mm), <em>approved </em>aerial fire apparatus access roads shall be provided. For purposes of this section, the highest roof surface shall be determined by measurement to the eave of a pitched roof, the intersection of the roof to the exterior wall, or the top of parapet walls, whichever is greater.</span></span></span></span></span></p>
        
        <p style="margin-left:80px; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><strong><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Exception: </span></span></span></strong><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Where <em>approved </em>by the <em>fire code official</em>, buildings of Type IA, Type IB or Type IIA construction equipped throughout with an <em>automatic sprinkler system </em>in accordance with Section 903.3.1.1 and having fire fighter access through an enclosed <em>stairway </em>with a Class I standpipe from the lowest level of fire department vehicle access to all roof surfaces.</span></span></span></span></span></p>
        
        <ol start="4" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Appendix E &ndash; Hazardous Categories.</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="5" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Appendix F &ndash; Hazard Ranking.</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="6" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Appendix G &ndash; Cryogenic Fluids &ndash; Weight and Volume Equivalents.</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="7" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Appendix H &ndash; Hazardous Materials Management Plan (HMM<s>O</s><u>P</u>) and Hazardous Materials Inventory Statement (HMIS) Instructions.</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="8" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Appendix I &ndash; Fire Protection Systems &ndash; Noncompliant Conditions</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-roman">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Appendix J &ndash; Building Information Sign.</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="10" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Appendix N &ndash; Indoor Trade Shows and Exhibitions</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 16, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, July 30, 2025</p><p>ORD C36695 Section 4</p></form>
        </div>
        </div></td>
        	</tr>
        </table>
